      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{|x|\\sqrt{2({x}^{2}+1)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
